    {
        "text": "A long time ago, Gerald used to look up at the night sky when he needed a breather after killing."
    },
    {
        "text": "The sky is an oppressive black. The campfire has gone out, and even the embers have cooled."
    },
    {
        "text": "Bloodied mercenaries wipe away the dirt from their faces, gazing at their equally battered comrades, briefly pondering questions they hardly have the luxury to think about."
    },
    {
        "text": "Can Sarkaz like them truly hope for a happy life?"
    },
    {
        "text": "He once believed that the day would come when the Sarkaz rebuilt their home, but he feels more helpless with each passing day."
    },
    {
        "text": "They have shed too much blood. They will run out of blood before their monarch's vision comes true."
    },
    {
        "text": "Eventually, Gerald abandoned Kazdel, bringing along those gasping for breath, running from the land they once fought to the death for."
    },
    {
        "text": "They hid from the world, ultimately finding a place that would take them. All they wanted was a normal, peaceful life."
    },
    {
        "text": "The dream came true, once."
    },
    {
        "text": "When did life turn bitter and oppressive?"
    },
    {
        "text": "It is like a fine dish on the table that no one has tasted."
    },
    {
        "text": "It has gone bad through no one's doing."
    },
    {
        "text": "If only blood can end this all..."
    },
    {
        "text": "Then there is only one thing left to do."
    },
    {
        "tag": "dialog"
    },
    {
